(6601638, 984194, 132251, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by IAmEliKatz:</b></div><hr/><i> Dammit, ya beat me again!<br/> <br/>Funky Lock, and whats with the empty bottles? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Damn right, I beat you! <br/>It is my wine rack. I keep some empties on the bottle to make it look "fuller" than I can afford...</td>', 'Originally posted by IAmEliKatz: Dammit, ya beat me again! Funky Lock, and whats with the empty bottles?   Damn right, I beat you! It is my wine rack. I keep some empties on the bottle to make it look "fuller" than I can afford...', '2011-11-23 05:53:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6601639, 983683, 49018, '<td valign="top">This reminds me I should pay my credit card before strangers come knocking :D<br/>Good angle and pretty good, out of the box, idea. I wonder if it might have worked more drammatically by further boosting the difference in luminance between inside and outside. Perhaps by  making the door and generally the inside considerably darker, or by taking a long exposure while shining a very strong light over the crack of the door, so you have spillage of light.<br/>The overprocessed hands goes well with the idea of a not human creature, but for me it would probably be even more disturbing the contrast between that claws and a normal skin tone, auntie Polly''s little secret kind of thing (but admittedly it would be difficult to balance things up so that would look convincing rather than halfcooked).<br/> <br/>Good stuff Joshua !<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-11-23 05:55:11.</i></td>', 'This reminds me I should pay my credit card before strangers come knocking :DGood angle and pretty good, out of the box, idea. I wonder if it might have worked more drammatically by further boosting the difference in luminance between inside and outside. Perhaps by  making the door and generally the inside considerably darker, or by taking a long exposure while shining a very strong light over the crack of the door, so you have spillage of light.The overprocessed hands goes well with the idea of a not human creature, but for me it would probably be even more disturbing the contrast between that claws and a normal skin tone, auntie Polly''s little secret kind of thing (but admittedly it would be difficult to balance things up so that would look convincing rather than halfcooked). Good stuff Joshua !', '2011-11-23 05:54:14.000000', '2011-11-23 05:55:11.000000', 0),
